1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,700
This is Pocket Proof, a local AI optimization lab running on a native Arm64 Apple M5.
Choose one of three public-domain video presets.

2
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:17,780
Each preview maps to checksum-pinned audio, a reference transcript,
and a recorded license in the SQLite catalog.

3
00:00:17,780 --> 00:00:27,800
The benchmark runs one warm-up and five alternating measurements per profile,
then streams the real lane and run number into Judge Mode.

4
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:37,950
The controlled change is FP16 to Q4_0 weights, using the same native CPU binary,
clip, thread count, and decoder.

5
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:49,000
On the featured clip, Q4_0 is 1.59× faster, uses 43.7% less peak memory,
and makes the model 70.2% smaller.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:00,050
Across three licensed clips and 30 measured processes, median paired speedup is 1.55×,
with a bootstrap interval from 1.49× to 1.62×.

7
00:01:00,050 --> 00:01:11,500
Corpus WER changes from 6.9% to 8.3% because the noisy Apollo clip
changes one additional word.

8
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:23,050
KleidiAI did not improve this M5 configuration, so it remains negative evidence.
Every run stays immutable and exportable.
